Q1.
CONTEXT (where the removed facts print): Both tunes satisfy the bias criteria: the pseudo-experiment means give $\chi^2=\fvval{f1-g18-chi2}$ ($p=\fvval{f1-g18-p}$) and \fvval{f1-ar23-chi2} ($p=\fvval{f1-ar23-p}$), respectively, with $|z|\leq\fvval{f1-zmax-ceil}$ in every cell of the means and closures. The tests assess bias, not coverage: only event counts fluctuate, with systematic parameters fixed, so interval widths cannot be tested. \begin{table*}[tb] \caption{Fake-data tests on the sixteen cells: $\chi^2$ (16 degrees of freedom), $p$ and the cells with $|z|>\fvval{trig-z}$, against $C_{\mathrm{total}}+C_{\mathrm{resp}}$ and against $C_{\mathrm{total}}$, each without the truth's own generator component where the second column says so ($-$).} \label{tab:fd16} \centering\scriptsize\setlength{\tabcolsep}{3pt} \begin{tabular}{@{}llrrlrrl@{}} \toprule & & \multicolumn{3}{c}{$C_{\mathrm{total}}+C_{\mathrm{resp}}$} & \multicolumn{3}{c}{$C_{\mathrm{total}}$} \\ \cmidrule(lr){3-5}\cmidrule(l){6-8} Truth & Cov. & $\chi^2$ & $p$ & cells & $\chi^2$ & $p$ & cells \\ \midrule simulation prior & full & \fvval{f0b-nominal-chi2} & $\fvval{f0b-nominal-p}$ & \fvval{f0b-nominal-cells} & \fvval{f0-nominal-chi2} & $\fvval{f0-nominal-p}$ & \fvval{f0-nominal-cells} \\ Tune~v1, hybrid & full & \fvval{f0b-A7_mnvtune-chi2} & $\fvval{f0b-A7_mnvtune-p}$ & \fvval{f0b-A7_mnvtune-cells} & \fvval{f0-A7_mnvtune-chi2} & $\fvval{f0-A7_mnvtune-p}$ & \fvval{f0-A7_mnvtune-cells} \\ GENIE CV, hybrid & full & \fvval{f0b-A7_genie_cv-chi2} & $\fvval{f0b-A7_genie_cv-p}$ & \fvval{f0b-A7_genie_cv-cells} & \fvval{f0-A7_genie_cv-chi2} & $\fvval{f0-A7_genie_cv-p}$ & \fvval{f0-A7_genie_cv-cells} \\ GENIE + MEC, hybrid & $-$GENIE + MEC & \fvval{f0b-A7_genie_mec-chi2} & $\fvval{f0b-A7_genie_mec-p}$ & \fvval{f0b-A7_genie_mec-cells} & \fvval{f0-A7_genie_mec-chi2} & $\fvval{f0-A7_genie_mec-p}$ & \fvval{f0-A7_genie_mec-cells} \\ GENIE + MEC, $(\Eavail,W)$ shape & $-$GENIE + MEC & \fvval{f0b-W2-chi2} & $\fvval{f0b-W2-p}$ & \fvval{f0b-W2-cells} & \fvval{f0-W2-chi2} & $\fvval{f0-W2-p}$ & \fvval{f0-W2-cells} \\ NuWro, hybrid & $-$NuWro & \fvval{f0b-A7_nuwro-chi2} & $\fvval{f0b-A7_nuwro-p}$ & \fvval{f0b-A7_nuwro-cells} & \fvval{f0-A7_nuwro-chi2} & $\fvval{f0-A7_nuwro-p}$ & \fvval{f0-A7_nuwro-cells} \\ NuWro, $\Eavail$ shape & $-$NuWro & \fvval{f0b-W1-chi2} & $\fvval{f0b-W1-p}$ & \fvval{f0b-W1-cells} & \fvval{f0-W1-chi2} & $\fvval{f0-W1-p}$ & \fvval{f0-W1-cells} \\ NuWro, $(\pT,\pPar,\Eavail)$ shape & $-$NuWro & \fvval{f0b-W3-chi2} & $\fvval{f0b-W3-p}$ & \fvval{f0b-W3-cells} & \fvval{f0-W3-chi2} & $\fvval{f0-W3-p}$ & \fvval{f0-W3-cells} \\ NuWro, closure & $-$NuWro & \fvval{f0b-closure_nuwro-chi2} & $\fvval{f0b-closure_nuwro-p}$ & \fvval{f0b-closure_nuwro-cells} & \fvval{f0-closure_nuwro-chi2} & $\fvval{f0-closure_nuwro-p}$ & \fvval{f0-closure_nuwro-cells} \\ GiBUU, $\Eavail$ shape & $-$GiBUU & \fvval{f0b-stage0c_gibuu-chi2} & $\fvval{f0b-stage0c_gibuu-p}$ & \fvval{f0b-stage0c_gibuu-cells} & \fvval{f0-stage0c_gibuu-chi2} & $\fvval{f0-stage0c_gibuu-p}$ & \fvval{f0-stage0c_gibuu-cells} \\ GiBUU, hybrid & $-$GiBUU & \fvval{f0b-A7_gibuu-chi2} & $\fvval{f0b-A7_gibuu-p}$ & \fvval{f0b-A7_gibuu-cells} & \fvval{f0-A7_gibuu-chi2} & $\fvval{f0-A7_gibuu-p}$ & \fvval{f0-A7_gibuu-cells} \\ synthetic $q_3$ tilt & full & \fvval{f0b-q3-chi2} & $\fvval{f0b-q3-p}$ & \fvval{f0b-q3-cells} & \fvval{f0-q3-chi2} & $\fvval{f0-q3-p}$ & \fvval{f0-q3-cells} \\ \bottomrule \end{tabular} \end{table*} Under the reported covariance, without the GiBUU component for the two GiBUU truths, the bias is listed at the GiBUU $\Eavail$ shape (cell R06, $z=\fvval{f0b-stage0c_gibuu-zmax}$), at the GiBUU hybrid truth ($p=\fvval{f0b-A7_gibuu-p}$; cells \fvval{f0b-A7_gibuu-cells}) and at the synthetic $q_3$ tilt ($p=\fvval{f0b-q3-p}$): the reported uncertainty does not cover the fake-data bias at these GiBUU-like truths or at the $q_3$ tilt. The $\chi^2$ of Table~\ref{tab:gen16} uses the full covariance, whose correlations the error bars do not show.} \label{fig:ratio16} \end{figure*} \begin{table}[tb] \caption{$\chi^2$ and its number of degrees of freedom of each prediction against the sixteen-cell result, under $C_{\mathrm{total}}+C_{\mathrm{resp}}+V_g$, with $V_g$ the prediction's finite-sample (diagonal) covariance; shape-only $\chi^2$ frees the normalization.} \label{tab:gen16} \centering\scriptsize \begin{tabular}{@{}lcc@{}} \toprule Prediction & $\chi^2$ and ndf & shape-only \\ \midrule \fvval{label-gcv} & \fvval{g-gcv-total-chi2int}/\fvval{g-gcv-total-ndf} & \fvval{g-gcv-shape_only-chi2int}/\fvval{g-gcv-shape_only-ndf} \\ \fvval{label-gmec} & \fvval{g-gmec-total-chi2int}/\fvval{g-gmec-total-ndf} & \fvval{g-gmec-shape_only-chi2int}/\fvval{g-gmec-shape_only-ndf} \\ \fvval{label-nuwro} & \fvval{g-nuwro-total-chi2int}/\fvval{g-nuwro-total-ndf} & \fvval{g-nuwro-shape_only-chi2int}/\fvval{g-nuwro-shape_only-ndf} \\ \fvval{label-gibuu} & \fvval{g-gibuu-total-chi2int}/\fvval{g-gibuu-total-ndf} & \fvval{g-gibuu-shape_only-chi2int}/\fvval{g-gibuu-shape_only-ndf} \\ \fvval{label-tune} & \fvval{g-tune-total-chi2int}/\fvval{g-tune-total-ndf} & \fvval{g-tune-shape_only-chi2int}/\fvval{g-tune-shape_only-ndf} \\ \bottomrule \end{tabular} \end{table} Weakening only the flux correlations by \fvval{sens-alpha-pct}\,\% lowers the $\chi^2$ of the 16-cell predictions by \fvval{sens-flux-fall-lo}--\fvval{sens-flux-fall-hi}\,\%.
BEFORE (Sec. I's paragraph on the result's limitations, accepted as correct): The result has three limitations, each stated with it. Interval coverage has not been validated. At two held-out GENIE~v3 truths, a bias test finds the estimator's bias below the reported uncertainty in every cell, but does not test interval widths. In a fake-data study at \fvval{f0b-all-truths} truths, the reported uncertainty does not cover the estimator's bias at the GiBUU-like truths or at a synthetic $q_{3}$ tilt (Sec.~\ref{sec:fd16}). The generator $\chi^{2}$ depends on the flux correlations: weakening only them by \fvval{sens-alpha-pct}\,\% lowers the $\chi^{2}$ of the sixteen-cell predictions by \fvval{sens-flux-fall-lo}--\fvval{sens-flux-fall-hi}\,\% (Sec.~\ref{sec:gen16}).
AFTER: Interval coverage has not been validated. The bias tests, the fake-data study and the dependence of the generator $\chi^{2}$ on the flux correlations are given with the result (Secs.~\ref{sec:fd16} and~\ref{sec:gen16}).

Q2.
CONTEXT (where the removed facts print): The Limitations subsection: The limitations of these results are stated with the results they qualify, in Secs.~\ref{sec:method}--\ref{sec:result16}, and those of the calibrated tests in the companion note. The principal ones are these. The two-dimensional covariance has not been independently validated, and its coverage has not been tested (Sec.~\ref{sec:uq2d}). The three- and four-observable central values lack intervals of validated coverage (Sec.~\ref{sec:central}). The sixteen-cell result also has total uncertainties, whose coverage is not validated; Sec.~\ref{sec:fd16} reports the fake-data tests of the estimator's bias. Four of the sixteen cells, \fvval{h2-lowstab-cells}, have a stability of \fvval{h2-lowstab-min}--\fvval{h2-lowstab-max}: of the simulated signal events generated in such a cell and reconstructed, only that fraction is reconstructed in the same cell. The note's calibrated tests reject hybrid nulls, conditionally on the simulation's hadronic response, and the rejections carry over to the generator predictions themselves only under a bound on the residual below the fine grid, which has not been shown. Their calibration is valid to the extent that the simulated chain reproduces the analysis of the data (\nsec{sec:joint5d-conditions}). They are not physical exclusions of the generators, and they show no evidence of additional discrimination beyond matched coarse projections.
BEFORE (the Scope paragraph, accepted as correct): \emph{Scope.} The findings are those of one OmniFold implementation on one data set, for the observables, configurations, and deformations tested, rather than of multidimensional OmniFold in general. The three- and four-observable results are central values without intervals of validated coverage: the output of the joint-test estimator of Sec.~\ref{sec:method}, with the observable definitions, simulated detector response, background treatment, and regularization given there. The sixteen-cell result of Sec.~\ref{sec:result16} also has total uncertainties, whose coverage is not validated. The companion note also gives simulation-calibrated tests of the generator predictions; they test hybrid null hypotheses, are calibrated within the implemented simulation model, and are not physical exclusions of the generators. They show no evidence of additional discrimination beyond matched coarse projections.
AFTER: \emph{Scope.} The findings are those of one OmniFold implementation on one data set, for the observables, configurations, and deformations tested, rather than of multidimensional OmniFold in general. The limitations are listed in Sec.~\ref{sec:limitations}.

