Q5.
CONTEXT (where the removed facts print): The note's release appendix: "The package, about \SI{16}{MB} of sufficient inputs, reproduces the joint-test $p$ values, decisions, robustness labels and power results; the same results in the reading with the recovered pseudo-experiments added to the calibration and the variant shifts recomputed on all draws (\S\ref{sec:joint5d-lost}); the matched coarse-projection comparison (\S\ref{sec:joint5d-projections}); and the fine-grid $L_2$ ratios of condition~(i) (\S\ref{sec:joint5d-conditions})." "RC7 supports replay of the higher-dimensional inference from sufficient inputs, but not extraction from the archived pseudo-experiment products, event-level unfolding, or the quoted closure, bias and covariance-status measurements." The paper's Sec. central quotes no numbers, and the paper quotes no multiplier scan.
BEFORE (the Data Availability statement, accepted as correct): The input data and simulation are the MINERvA open-data AnaTuples, released under CC0~\cite{MINERvA:OpenData}. This analysis used an earlier production of that release; its 2,374 input files are identified by SHA256 checksum in the records cited in \napp{app:release}. A candidate release package of about \SI{16}{MB}, not yet deposited, requires only numpy, scipy, and matplotlib. It recomputes every $p$ value, decision, robustness result, and power figure of the joint tests and the numbers quoted in Sec.~\ref{sec:central}, and it regenerates the analysis note's figures of the joint-test null distributions and the $(\Eavail,W)$ map. The other quoted numbers, except the multiplier scan, and the event-level processing require the archived analysis products, the open-data AnaTuples, and the generator samples produced for this analysis; \napp{app:release} states what each part of the release does and does not reproduce. \pubhold{deposit identifier and access route, after the separately authorized release decision.}
AFTER: The input data and simulation are the MINERvA open-data AnaTuples, released under CC0~\cite{MINERvA:OpenData}. This analysis used an earlier production of that release; its 2,374 input files are identified by SHA256 checksum in the records cited in \napp{app:release}. A candidate release package of about \SI{16}{MB}, not yet deposited, requires only numpy, scipy, and matplotlib, and regenerates the analysis note's figures of the joint-test null distributions and the $(\Eavail,W)$ map. The other quoted numbers and the event-level processing require the archived analysis products, the open-data AnaTuples, and the generator samples produced for this analysis; \napp{app:release} states what each part of the release does and does not reproduce. \pubhold{deposit identifier and access route, after the separately authorized release decision.}

